| Sent message may have failed | `./awt effect show <id>`, then ask a person |
| Check workspace health | `./awt doctor` |
| Commit the task dir (person asked) | `./awt save "message"` |
| Task finished | `./awt status done` |

## Syntax

```
./awt state --now "T" --next "T" [--scope S]
./awt note "T"
./awt decide "CHOICE" --why "T" [--supersedes ID] [--tag T]...
./awt ask "T"
./awt answer q-1a2b3c4d "T"
./awt ref TARGET --title "T" [--why "T"] [--kind K] [--no-access]
./awt capture --from SRC --title "T" [--ref URL] [FILE]
./awt supersede docs/old.md docs/new.md [--why "T"]
./awt status active|paused|done
./awt find "term"
./awt effect plan --target T (--body FILE | --run CMD) [--class additive|overwrite] [--snapshot CMD] [--verify CMD] [--after ID]... [--again] [--why T]
./awt effect show ID
./awt effect apply ID --target T [--timeout SECONDS]
./awt effect mark ID sent|not-sent|dropped [--ref URL] [--why T]
```

Example, manual Slack message (normal case):

```
./awt effect plan --target "slack:#eng" --body outbox/release-note.md
./awt effect mark e-3c91d0aa sent --ref https://example.slack.com/archives/C1/p1
```

Example, scripted send with check:

```
./awt effect plan --target "jira:TKT-1" --body outbox/c.md --run 'jira-cli comment TKT-1 "$(cat "$AWT_BODY")"' --verify 'jira-cli show TKT-1 | grep -q done'
```

`apply` is gated by a permission prompt for a person. Do not run it without approval. Each `plan` prints the exact next command: copy it.

## Refusals

Every refusal prints `error:` and `fix:`. Read the `fix:` first.

| Refusal | Meaning | Do |
|---|---|---|
| Text over cap | Field too long. Nothing was written. | Write detail to `docs/<name>.md`; put a short summary and the path in the field. Do not split into many rows. |
| Empty text | Blank after strip. | Supply text. |
| Identical state | `state` for that scope matches the current one. | Nothing to record. Move on. If work changed, say what changed. |
| Secret match (names a pattern) | A field holds a credential. Nothing written. No bypass exists. | Remove the secret, refer to it by name or location. If you cannot tell where it is, STOP and ask a person. |
| Unknown id (exit 4) | Wrong id for `answer`, `--supersedes`, `--after`, `effect`. | `./awt list <section>` and copy the id. |
| Already answered / already superseded | Duplicate action. | Use the current id the `fix:` names. |
| Path escapes the root | `--body` or `supersede` path resolves outside the task dir. | Copy the file into `outbox/` or `docs/` and retry. |
| `apply`: target mismatch | `--target` differs from the plan. | Re-run with the exact target from `effect show`. Never edit the plan to match. |
| `apply`: body changed | Body file edited after planning. | Re-plan. Show the person the new body: they approved the old one. |
| `apply`: manual effect | No `--run`. A person sends. | Show the body path, wait, then `effect mark <id> sent`. |
| `apply`: `--after` not sent | A prerequisite is not `sent`. | Resolve that effect first. |
| `plan`: open `unknown` on target | An earlier send on this target may have happened. | STOP and ask a person. Do not add `--again`. |
| `plan`: same key, dropped | Person dropped this exact send. | Only if a person wants it again: `--again`. |
| `overwrite` without `--snapshot` | No way back. | Add `--snapshot CMD`, or ask whether the action should be `additive`. |
| `status done` refused | Lists open questions and effects (`planned`, `claimed`, `unknown`). | Resolve each. For questions, a person must answer. For `unknown`, STOP and ask. Never mark `sent` or `dropped` to get past it. |
| `mark`: effect is `claimed`, pid alive | A send is running now. | Wait. |
| Exit 3 | No write permission. | Give the printed command to a person. |
| Exit 4, no `.awt/` | Not in a task. | `cd` to the task dir or pass `--dir`. Do not run `init` unless told. |

## Effect states

| State | You may | You must not |
|---|---|---|
| `planned` | Show the person; wait for approval; `mark dropped` if the person cancels | Send it yourself |
| `claimed` | Wait | `mark` anything |
| `sent` | Proceed; cite `--ref` if known | Plan the same send again |
| `unknown` | Run `effect show <id>`, report to a person, wait for them | Resend. Plan on that target. Mark it yourself. Run `status done`. |
| `dropped` | Move on | Revive without a person asking |
| `conflict` | Report to a person | Mark it |

`unknown` means the message may already be out. Resending can duplicate it. Only a person who has checked the real target may run `mark <id> sent` or `mark <id> not-sent`. `not-sent` makes it `planned` again for another attempt; the person decides that, not you.

`--again` is not a retry. It creates a new, separate send that bypasses the duplicate check. A failed or `unknown` send is never retried with `--again`. Use it only when a person wants a deliberate second identical message.

## Subagents

Worker, with a brief:
- Skip `./awt resume`. Read the brief.
- Write output to `docs/<brief>.out.md`. Never name a file starting with REPORT, SUMMARY, FINDINGS or ANALYSIS: Claude Code refuses those for subagents.
- Use `note`, `decide`, `ref`, `capture`, `ask`: parallel writes are safe.
- Do not run `state`, `status`, `effect apply` or `effect mark`. Do not write a handoff.
- Plan effects only if the brief says so. Never send.

Orchestrator:
- Owns `state` and `status`. Run `./awt state` once after collecting worker output, with `--next` naming the next step.
- Links worker files from `state` text by path (`docs/<brief>.out.md`).

## Big tasks: relay

If `./relay` exists and the work splits into parts, do not run them all in one session. Write a plan file (`./relay help` shows the format) with small units, a cheap model for reading, and a `check` command wherever a test can decide. Show the person the plan and `./relay run <plan>`, then stop. Afterwards `./awt resume` shows the result. Workers cannot send anything.

## Wrong moves

- Editing or deleting anything under `.awt/`. Use verbs. A bad row is quarantined, not fatal.
- Copying a page or thread you can link: use `ref`. Use `capture` only when no link works.
- Writing a second handoff such as `docs/HANDOFF.md`. `state` is the handoff.
- Sending directly (curl, `gh`, `slack` CLI, API call) instead of through `effect`.
- Putting long text in `--now`, `--why`, `note`. Write `docs/`, reference the path.
- Using `--again` or a fresh `plan` to get around an `unknown` effect.
- Re-asking or re-researching without `./awt find` first.'''

